@prefix sh: <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .
@prefix test: <http://test.example.com/> .
@prefix : <http://test.example.com/shapes/> .

# sh:xone over TWO node-shape disjuncts.
# Phase 3B forcing-function fixture: validates that XoneConstraint
# participates in Shape.minQuery alongside AndConstraint (same fix; see
# ADR-009).
#
# K-02 DEFERRAL (carried forward from P2C-A, locked in P3B per Q-22):
# Trav-SHACL's engine currently treats sh:xone disjuncts as a conjunction
# at the rule-pattern body level — it accepts a focus when BOTH disjuncts
# match (the SHACL §4.6.4 strict "exactly one" requirement is NOT
# enforced). Strict exactly-one would require engine support for counting
# satisfied disjuncts in the interleave step, deferred until
# sh:ValidationReport sub-result emission lands (Phase 4+).
#
# Engine-faithful ground truth (per inspection of tests/data/test.ttl;
# matches case3 sh:and partitioning):
#   Instance0: property1✓ property2✗  → invalid (≠ both match)
#   Instance1: property1✓ property2✓  → valid (engine: both match;
#                                              strict-xone WOULD be invalid)
#   Instance2: property1✓ property2✓  → valid (same caveat)
#   Instance3: property1✓ property2✗  → invalid
#   Instance4: property1✗ property2✓  → invalid (engine: ≠ both match;
#                                                strict-xone WOULD be valid)
#   Instance5: property1✓ property2✓  → valid (same caveat)
#   Instance6: property1✓ property2✓  → valid (same caveat)
#   → valid: {1, 2, 5, 6}; invalid: {0, 3, 4}
#
# Strict-xone partition (for the deferred fix's future reference):
#   valid: {0, 3, 4} (exactly one disjunct satisfied)
#   invalid: {1, 2, 5, 6} (both disjuncts satisfied — violates exactly-one)
# This is intentionally DIFFERENT from engine-faithful and DIFFERENT from
# case3 sh:and. ADR-009 §Consequences pins K-02 as the deferred work.

:HasProperty1 a sh:NodeShape ;
  sh:property [
    sh:path test:property1 ;
    sh:minCount 1
  ] .

:HasProperty2 a sh:NodeShape ;
  sh:property [
    sh:path test:property2 ;
    sh:minCount 1
  ] .

:ClassA a sh:NodeShape ;
  sh:targetClass test:ClassA ;
  sh:xone (
    [ sh:node :HasProperty1 ]
    [ sh:node :HasProperty2 ]
  ) .
